\ Benchmark: clamp-sum loop (less-synthetic workload).
\
\ A compiled `while` loop sums a threshold-branched transform of each index. The
\ inner `dup 500 < [ 3 * ] [ 2 * ] if` is a same-type i64 merge feeding
\ arithmetic, living inside a compiled loop body -- the exact "if inside a loop"
\ shape the branchless IR_COND select must stay correct in. Unlike the micro
\ benchmark there is just one merge per iteration amid ordinary loop work, so it
\ checks the optimization does not regress a realistic mix.
\
\ Run with ONEZ_PROTOTYPE_COND_SELECT unset (baseline) vs set (IR_COND select).
\ Prints elapsed nanoseconds and a checksum (identical on/off proves correctness).

use "time" ;

clamp-sum: ( n -- sum ) [
  0
  [ over 0 > ]
  [ over dup 500 < [ 3 * ] [ 2 * ] if + swap 1 - swap ]
  while
  nip
] ;

clamp-sum: compile!

monotonic-nanos 80000000 clamp-sum swap monotonic-nanos swap -
"clamp-sum ns=" print inspect print-line
"clamp-sum sum=" print inspect print-line
